Z||000000||gkozlov||10-05-2000||08:14 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wheels_1.jpg"> <BR>The wheel on the left is of a kit car (Fiero)I saw on the net and the one on the right was on a Indy for sale on Ebay a while back. gkozlov<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||10-05-2000||09:47 AM||||The one on the left was made by Centerline. The one on the right was made by American Racing. I don't think they make those styles anymore. You could try looking them up on the internet and see if they have anything close. IRM use to sell the centerlines but It's not listed in their recent catalog.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||10-05-2000||11:48 AM||||Progressive also made a wheel like the one on the right. Had a set on my 85 GT. <BR>I think they're out of production, too.<BR>Look at Dodge Daytona wheels. They are similar. The bolt pattern is the same as a Fiero, but I believe the offset is different. I've seen them on an 86 or 87 GT. They <I>might</I> rub on an 88. I've heard that the spring "hats" on the rear of an 88 are larger. I've also heard that coil-overs will remedy that.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (soon to receive transplant.)<BR>88 "pretzeled" Formula <P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||gkozlov||10-05-2000||05:29 PM||||Does anybody know where I could get a set cheap? <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||10-05-2000||08:13 PM||||I have a set of the wheels on the left, but they have been powdercoated yellow. And I think one is cracked because it leaks between the 2 pieces (2 piece rims). They are 16x8 and the front and rears have different offsets. They are Centerlines.||||reg||1
Z||000005||gkozlov||10-05-2000||08:25 PM||||SCCA FIERO, Shipping would probably cost a small fortune from Ohio to Alabama. Just out of curiosity how much are you asking for them?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||10-05-2000||08:54 PM||||I hadn't really thought about selling them to tell you the truth. I need to take the tire off that one to see how big the crack is... might not be repairable. I wouldn't want to sell you a bad wheel. I also forgot to tell you that two others look like they have hit a curb. The lip is kinda munched on them.<P>BTW, I live in Utah, not Ohio.||||reg||1
